  "judge": {
    "dimensions": [
      {
        "name": "Correctness",
        "score": 8,
        "rationale": "The spec mocks GitHub at the dashboard's example.net API base to return one open PR whose head ref is cms/posts/<slug> for a real, published, non-fixture post, seeds the token via the decap-cms-user localStorage entry, clicks Refresh, then scopes to the `li` card containing that entry's Decap link and asserts the 'preview draft' link is visible with an exact href of https://preview-pr4242.<CMS_APEX>/blog/<slug>/ and target=_blank, plus that /pulls was actually requested. That is a card-to-open-PR association with origin and /blog/<slug>/ destination, not a bare href check, and it uses li cards and /blog/ rather than role=row or /preview/. Gaps: the Published-OFF explanatory-span branch is explained in comments but never asserted, and the date-prefix-stripping slug derivation and 'preview draft' link name are untested assumptions since no browser run occurred."
      },
      {
        "name": "Routing",
        "score": 9,
        "rationale": "Tagged @admin-read via describe options, read-only (mocked network, never clicks Save/Publish), no viewport pin, so both admin projects can run it natively. Posts guard uses cap.keepsBaseCollection(SITE_ROOT, 'posts') as a describe-level test.skip before any Posts usage. All navigation is a relative page.goto('/admin/index-local.html') against baseURL and it enters Posts via the collection link rather than an entry page, avoiding the entry-to-entry publish trap. No project-name skip. Minor: the registry lint acceptance of the inline guard is unconfirmed."
      },
      {
        "name": "Restraint",
        "score": 10,
        "rationale": "The staged diff contains exactly one new file, e2e/cms-posts-list-preview-link.spec.js; no harness, base, example spec, or PLATFORM_META_SPECS changes."
      },
      {
        "name": "Explanation",
        "score": 9,
        "rationale": "The reply states up front that the test was not run in a browser and why (no Playwright, Jekyll, or decap-server), lists exactly what ran (node --check and all seven check-spec.js modes, with mutation checks proving the checker can fail), lists what was not run (the Playwright test, admin-tag-lint and base-collections-guard-registry tests), flags the first-real-run precondition, and explains what the test proves. It clearly distinguishes AST validation from a browser pass and makes no unsupported pass claim."
      }
    ],
    "overall": 8.8
  },
